{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1789691450122383224,"compiled_state":{"alias":"stable-jobless-coot","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"4f12815e9a0b0cee5ded72d73e22256115e10c87","key_id":null,"kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: f5ac-391c-ec70-4fa9","material: 3a474d38284c9218","material-part: children 647ea2107ca5072f 0","material-part: description 66b54d01912aea6b 2393","material-part: description_boxes 7879981d4f226a8f 0","material-part: file_impact 003ffa614d5e4a28 0","material-part: ticket_id e5f8b892a5bab826 19","model: bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 2","review-phase: planning","rebar-version: 0.13.1","regver: aa61189569d34126","verified-at-sha:4f12815e9a0b0cee5ded72d73e22256115e10c87","currency-basis: fail-safe"],"material_fingerprint":"3a474d38284c9218","merged_log_commit":"4f12815e9a0b0cee5ded72d73e22256115e10c87","principal":"9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65","signature":null,"signed_at":1789669165837942617}},"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"859bc1d9e4f23f7122bbb19bde391dfe47b9415c230484deec2fffc7c41898e8","event_uuid":"f84ae7b2-d61b-45ba-975c-1cc1cb6b248a","position":{"commit_sha":"b2e75599e299b638c40012999e1eed91c4c83b56","position":"1789668213464836418-f84ae7b2-d61b-45ba-975c-1cc1cb6b248a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d5d889337e43355eb217b1ccb7f98aed118f6743931a3e926f0968d9f2454d66","event_uuid":"c4441082-9a7a-47e4-bd7b-08606572de56","position":{"commit_sha":"be0caf24df009494040e5ffb54556b5eb37b0642","position":"1789669165838209719-c4441082-9a7a-47e4-bd7b-08606572de56"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"559d5a5684fd7134401ed0fa907b44bf8bc13f2d9ab19652139515a8ad8adbb8","event_uuid":"945a3742-308b-4365-88a5-39e65c1e3e1b","position":{"commit_sha":"e3d6b662a8d888f686721bf768d6c764a88cd878","position":"1789670280111438562-945a3742-308b-4365-88a5-39e65c1e3e1b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"532ab2e9ce5c56ee008a0be123d13f686c5cd72b823727b2350c0edffbc1fb04","event_uuid":"91aec344-b59d-41ba-81ea-22e90be826e8","position":{"commit_sha":"e3d6b662a8d888f686721bf768d6c764a88cd878","position":"1789670280198980922-91aec344-b59d-41ba-81ea-22e90be826e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"39ffc0af06f25ffc80a30f4b3b249d96b84f77f82d793524370f220b323cdabe","event_uuid":"8511115d-71b0-4156-8755-04e18de3c785","position":{"commit_sha":"583ce4ed2768bc888b2d628f4e6a68ab5cc41b1e","position":"1789672467583695284-8511115d-71b0-4156-8755-04e18de3c785"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Root cause confirmed — the gate measures the ticket store, not the code checkout\n\nInvestigation reproduced CI locally within pack-transfer variance: **648,346 KiB** local against Actions' **648,505 KiB**.\n\n### The pack is not the code\n\n| Fetch shape | size-pack KiB | Share of failing pack |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main-only, blobless, full history | 23,268 | 3.6% |\n| tickets-only, blobless, full history | 624,881 | 96.4% |\n| all-heads, blobless, full history | 648,346 | 100% (reproduces CI) |\n\n`.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml` checks out with `filter: blob:none` and `fetch-depth: 0`. The unbounded depth pulls every remote head, including `origin/tickets`. The authorship gate then measures that combined pack and fails closed.\n\nComposition of the failing pack by object type:\n\n```\nblob    count=5098    disk_kib=24605.6     3.8%\ncommit  count=296468  disk_kib=56059.5     8.6%\ntree    count=518053  disk_kib=553579.0   85.4%\n```\n\nTree objects are 85.4% of it, and the tickets-only blobless fetch contains **zero blobs**. This is the event-sourced ticket store's directory graph, which is exactly what an append-only store accumulates.\n\n### It is not a large file, and not organic growth\n\nThe four largest blobs across all heads total roughly 1.7 MiB; all blobs together are 24.0 MiB. No single-artifact removal can address an 85 MiB overage. The top 30 ticket tree objects are 9,514 KiB — 1.47% of the pack. The cost is the accumulation of 494,742 tree objects, not any one object.\n\n### The crossing was a discrete history event, not a growth curve\n\n| Point | size-pack KiB |\n|---|---:|\n| 2026-09-04 | 482,385 |\n| 2026-09-09 | 496,077 |\n| 2026-09-10 18:30Z | 496,938 |\n| **2026-09-10 19:00Z** | **598,124** |\n| 2026-09-17 12:57Z | 624,751 |\n\nBaseline growth is ~2.5 MiB/day before and ~3.9 MiB/day after. Between 18:30Z and 19:00Z on 2026-09-10 the pack gained **101,186 KiB in about 30 minutes**. The commit at the jump, `924a93f21edf6c4066339feeb7fff2294244d917` (`chore: sync events from rebar reconciler [run 34514936676]`), is not a descendant of the commit before it and makes **28,570 previously-unreachable commits** reachable, the oldest dating to 2026-08-29.\n\nThis matters for the fix: extrapolating a new limit from a growth rate would be fitting a line to a step.\n\n### This repository already learned this lesson\n\nThe Gerrit-side workflow carries an explicit note against the very gate that is failing here:\n\n```\nNOTE: there is deliberately NO pack-size gate here. A hard cap on the tickets\npack ... is guaranteed to be crossed eventually and, once crossed, casts Verified -1\non EVERY Gerrit change repo-wide until someone bumps the number.\n```\n\nThe scheduled authorship gate has the same property, differing only in blast radius. `d0bcd620278` already raised this limit once from 102400 to 563200 and described it as a temporary bridge; the comment still says to restore 102400. That is the second crossing of a cap whose input is an append-only store, which is the predicted behaviour rather than a surprise.\n\nThe limit is not single-sourced in a `.github/*-limit.txt` file. It lives in the workflow and is mirrored by a contract test at `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py:101`, so any change must move both.\n\n### Not done, and deliberately so\n\nThe reconciler behaviour that made run `34514936676` introduce 28,570 older commits non-linearly was not traced to source. The Git evidence establishes the event and its pack impact; the code path did not get read. Filed separately so it is not lost inside this gate fix.\n\nNo `git gc`, `repack`, `prune`, or `fsck` was run. All measurements come from fresh scratch clones.\n","timestamp":1789672467583695284}],"created_at":1789668213464836418,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Symptom\n\nThe scheduled `Verify Authorship Identity` workflow has failed on consecutive scheduled runs:\n\n- run 35192575898 at 2026-09-17T07:02:22Z\n- run 35224107600 at 2026-09-17T12:57:24Z (head `5b143d9b15ba45509757f125126132c34c9dfe53`)\n\nThe failing job is `verify-identity (authenticated-authorship gate)`; the failing step is \"Fail closed if the blobless checkout pack exceeds its limit\". The error is exact:\n\n```\ncheckout pack is 648505 KiB; limit is 563200 KiB\n```\n\nwith `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 563200` in the step environment. The overage is roughly 85 MiB, about 15% over the limit.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the authenticated-authorship gate. It fails **closed** by design, so while it is red the gate is not verifying authorship at all — it is aborting before it gets there. A gate that always fails provides no signal, and a standing red scheduled run trains readers to ignore it. Both scheduled runs on 2026-09-17 failed, so this is a persistent condition rather than a flake.\n\n## Investigation required before any fix\n\nThe limit is deliberately a fail-closed bound, so raising the number is a fix only if the growth is legitimate. The investigation must distinguish:\n\n1. **Legitimate growth** — the repository's blobless pack has grown organically past a bound that was set when the repo was smaller, and the bound needs to track repo size.\n2. **Debris** — a large blob, an accidentally committed artifact, or a packing regression inflated the pack. In that case raising the limit hides the real defect.\n\nEstablish which by measuring the pack's composition (largest objects and their paths) and by finding when the pack crossed the limit relative to the bound's last change. Do not change the limit before that question is answered.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The root cause is identified as either legitimate growth or specific debris, with the measurement that distinguishes them recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] If debris: the offending objects are named and removed or excluded, and the pack measures under the limit.\n- [ ] If legitimate growth: the bound is adjusted with a recorded rationale tying it to observed repository size, including headroom for expected growth.\n- [ ] A regression guard exists so the next approach to the limit is visible before the gate turns red.\n- [ ] `Verify Authorship Identity` passes on a scheduled run after the change lands.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"945a3742-308b-4365-88a5-39e65c1e3e1b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f5ac-391c-ec70-4fa9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Verify Authorship Identity fails closed: blobless checkout pack exceeded its limit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f84ae7b2-d61b-45ba-975c-1cc1cb6b248a","c4441082-9a7a-47e4-bd7b-08606572de56","945a3742-308b-4365-88a5-39e65c1e3e1b","91aec344-b59d-41ba-81ea-22e90be826e8","8511115d-71b0-4156-8755-04e18de3c785"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789691450122383224,"uuid":"9b50a32b-abce-44ff-9acd-17dd3bf9ae34"}